          "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSome of this material is in the chapter of <REF_0001> called\n``Easy consistency proofs''.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a formula of set theory.\nLet us use the convention that this notation implies that\nall the free variables in <MATH_0002> occur among <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a set.\nThe formula <MATH_0005> is the\nformula obtained from <MATH_0006> by replacing all the\n<MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> by <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010>,\nrespectively. So the formula\n<MATH_0011>\nis turned  into\n<MATH_0012>.\nThe formula <MATH_0013> is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>relativization of <MATH_0014>\nto <MATH_0015><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n\n",
